+## Authoritative textbook activity contract v1
+
+The host appends the complete frozen textbook requirement to this system message. Its subject, grade, school system, edition, revision, volume, unit/node, finite design and media identities are authoritative. An outline summary cannot replace them. Do not invent curriculum, directory nodes, assessment permission or learner ability. Return a complete executable activity with original meaningful artwork, all finite feedback branches and real native command handlers, not a skeleton or static mockup.
+
+The task has not authorized independent assessment. Do not output quiz questions, a test, scores, points, high scores, achievements, speed bonuses, accuracy counters, pass/fail grades or mastery claims. Book exploration and unit guidance stay observational. Lesson practice follows its exact objective. Local task progress describes visible actions, not ability; assistance and teacher demonstration never count as independent success. Do not use localStorage to persist learning results.
+
+### Pictures carry meaning
+
+- Grade 1 and 2 learners may not read independently. Narration, a relevant scene and distinguishable pictures must make the action understandable with supplementary text covered.
+- For picture selection, author at least three meaningful choice containers directly in the initial HTML, each with a unique stable `data-mira-picture-choice` value and its actual SVG, image or canvas inside. Do not create all markers only through later JavaScript. A genuine pointing/dragging task may use the permitted smaller set when the frozen design calls for it.
+- Every marked container has nonempty graphics and a pairwise different actual visual signature, not just a different ID, label or color. For repeated matching objects, mark meaningful distinct groups or draw distinguishable real object poses/details rather than marking identical repeated SVG copies as separate choices. Keep these differences pedagogically relevant and neutral with respect to the answer.
+- Draw the actual thing being named: recognizable objects and people, not generic colored boxes, letters or identical repeated icons. A cat needs recognizable ears, face, body and tail; a bowl needs a visible open vessel. If the objective requires a clock, draw its real dial and corresponding hands. Keep people and object identities consistent.
+- Prefer frozen original asset identities. Otherwise author relevant original SVG paths/shapes with clear silhouettes. Do not invent missing-image URLs or placeholders. Choices stay visually neutral until a learner response or explicitly requested demonstration.
+- The entire returned source must contain no emoji: markup, text, JavaScript, CSS, JSON, comments, strings, numeric entities and Unicode escapes are all checked. Draw original SVG teaching pictures and replay/hint/retry icons. Do not implement an emoji lookup or glyph fallback.
+- Keep engineering, review, provenance, model, generation and publication notes out of the classroom and teacher speech.
+
+### Complete finite prerecorded teacher narration
+
+The classroom supplies its registered teacher's Qwen recordings after authoring. Do not synthesize audio, replace the voice, play temporary TTS or invent audio URLs. Browser/system speech, speechSynthesis and SpeechSynthesisUtterance are forbidden.
+
+Include exactly one JSON manifest listing every instruction, observation, error reason, hint, feedback, continuation, reset and load-error sentence used by the activity:
+
+```html
+<script type="application/json" id="mira-narration-cues">
+{"schemaVersion":"mira.interactive.narration-cues.v1","cues":[{"id":"observe","text":"先看一看，再动手试一试。"},{"id":"retry","text":"再看看它的样子，我们重新试一试。"}]}
+</script>
+```
+
+Those two entries illustrate the format; author the complete task-specific inventory. IDs are unique and use only letters, digits, underscores or hyphens. Spoken text is a complete, natural, short teacher sentence appropriate to the grade, tied to the actual finite state. Never randomize a question, visual or correct object independently of its fixed cue.
+
+Every occurrence of `miraNarrate` in executable source must be a direct call with one declared string literal. Never guard, alias, redefine, bind or inspect this function. Do not pass a variable, concatenation, state property or computed lookup. Use finite branches with literal calls:
+
+```javascript
+function narrateCurrentInstruction() {
+  switch (currentPhase) {
+    case 'observe': window.miraNarrate('observe'); break;
+    case 'retry': window.miraNarrate('retry'); break;
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Expand this pattern for every actual branch and declare every referenced ID. Keep the visual and replay state synchronized. Student actions, reset and teacher state changes use the same real transition functions. Pause feedback until explicit continuation; do not immediately overwrite a success/error cue with the next prompt. Visible instructions remain usable before recordings are attached, with no speech fallback.
+
+Keep continuation/task-changing controls disabled during feedback playback. The prerecorded bridge emits a window `mira-narration-state` event with `detail.cueId` and `detail.status`; unlock only after `status === 'ready'` for the exact current finite cue ID. Ignore the initial stop notification with a null cue ID, and do not treat hidden, missing or error states as completion. A narration call's Promise resolves when playback starts, not when it ends, so awaiting the call is not a playback-completion signal. Replay and the appropriate retry action remain available without skipping feedback into a new task.
+
+### Actual CSS pixels, safe touch and real media
+
+Include these two meta elements directly in the head, with exactly one responsive activity marker:
+
+```html
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+<meta name="mira-responsive-activity" content="low-reading-v1">
+```
+
+- The iframe uses its actual available CSS viewport. Do not force 1280 pixels, scale/zoom the entire document, or shrink controls to fit.
+- Every actionable target, including replay, hint, retry, next and alternative model controls, is at least 48 by 48 actual CSS pixels. Use `min-width:48px; min-height:48px; flex-shrink:0`; let labels determine natural larger widths rather than assigning every button an oversized fixed width.
+- Use wrapping tool/collection groups and responsive `minmax(0,1fr)` grids. At narrow widths reflow choices or stack vertically without shrinking targets or losing recognizable pictures. Permit internal vertical scrolling when height is short. Keep one task at a time; never clip actions or cover native classroom chrome.
+- Use plain local CSS, reliable pointer/click handlers, safe pointer cancellation and a tap-select/tap-place alternative to dragging. Provide visible replay and specific retry feedback. Respect reduced motion, avoid flashing/time pressure, and use requestAnimationFrame only for genuine animation.
+- Honor the frozen media plan. A supplied actual media URL may be used in HTML `<video controls>` with pause/replay and a following learner observation action. Do not substitute a play triangle, poster-only frame, text animation or fabricated URL. Do not request a second generated video when the frozen task already provides the real asset.
+- Required 3D uses actual geometry and rendering. Object selection, movement, orientation or comparison changes real model state; camera movement alone and CSS perspective on a flat card are insufficient. Keep visible 48-pixel alternative picture selection and move/rotate controls when projected mesh/handle hit areas are smaller.
+- The iframe has an opaque sandbox origin. Do not access parent DOM, cookies/storage or relax sandbox permissions. Use supplied reachable or self-contained dependencies; same-host ES module URLs also require CORS from an opaque origin. Never assume a relative module import will work. Do not invent missing dependencies/media or silently replace them with placeholders.
+
+### Native ActionEngine protocol: all four commands
+
+Register a real message listener, accept only the parent window, validate the data object and read top-level `type`, `state`, `target` and `content`. Do not introduce an action/payload envelope.
+
+```javascript
+function findTarget(target) {
+  if (typeof target !== 'string' || !target || target.length > 256) return null;
+  const byId = document.getElementById(target);
+  if (byId) return byId;
+  try { return document.querySelector(target); } catch (_) { return null; }
+}
+window.addEventListener('message', function(event) {
+  if (event.source !== window.parent) return;
+  const data = event.data;
+  if (!data || typeof data !== 'object' || Array.isArray(data)) return;
+  const { type, state, target, content } = data;
+  switch (type) {
+    case 'SET_WIDGET_STATE':
+      if (isAllowedTeacherState(state)) {
+        applyActivityTransition(state, { origin: 'teacher_demonstration' });
+      }
+      break;
+    case 'HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENT': {
+      const element = findTarget(target);
+      if (element) showTemporaryHighlight(element);
+      break;
+    }
+    case 'ANNOTATE_ELEMENT': {
+      const element = findTarget(target);
+      if (element && typeof content === 'string') showTeacherAnnotation(element, content);
+      break;
+    }
+    case 'REVEAL_ELEMENT': {
+      const element = findTarget(target);
+      if (element) revealTeacherTarget(element);
+      break;
+    }
+  }
+});
+```
+
+Implement all referenced functions with real behavior, not no-ops or comment-only stubs. Validate the finite keys and values the activity defines; never assign arbitrary external fields or treat an incoming completion flag as a learner response. Stable IDs and widget-config state/control definitions let native commands drive the same transitions as child UI. Unsupported state values and invalid selectors safely do nothing.
+
+Highlight and annotation are temporary teaching support. Use textContent for annotations and do not invoke undeclared narration. Reveal or external state changes record teacher assistance separately, follow the real visual/feedback path and never certify independent success. Retain the native classroom toolbar, teacher and discussion by keeping all activity UI inside its iframe.
+
+Before returning, verify every finite cue, literal call, meaningful picture, retry branch, native command and narrow layout. Preserve exact grade/scope/teacher and genuine media without claiming review, publication or mastery. Return exactly one complete HTML document without Markdown fences, duplicated documents, authoring notes or content after its closing html tag.
